{"type":"message","id":"22259bd7","parentId":"830a4b0a","timestamp":"2026-06-02T10:02:49.221Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Can't search the web. But I have general knowledge about gout and purines. Let me answer from what I know:\n\nFor gout:\n- Chicken (鸡肉): Moderate purine content. Generally okay in moderation during non-acute phases. During an acute flare-up, it's better to limit intake. Skinless chicken breast is better.\n- Duck (鸭肉): Moderate-high purine content. Similar to chicken but slightly higher. During acute gout attacks, it's better to avoid. In remission, can eat in moderation.\n\nActually, let me check if I can use web_fetch on a reliable source.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_InT6VbG8Db1kvi1doRmE2732","name":"web_fetch","arguments":{"url":"https://baike.baidu.com/item/%E7%97%9B%E9%A3%8E%E9%A5%AE%E9%A3%9F","maxChars":3000}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":177,"output":344,"cacheRead":28800,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":29321,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780394562604}}
